<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sakai Tadashige</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1827">1827</a>–<a href="/years/1895">1895</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sakai Tadashige was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of Himeji Domain in Harima province. He served as tairo, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>'s great elder, at the very end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a>. Because of this office Himeji was treated as an enemy by the imperial side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a> of 1868, and the castle surrendered when besieged. The domain later became part of Hyogo Prefecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sakai-tadashige.jpg" alt="Sakai Tadashige" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sakai_Tadasige.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
